          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Asha's teacher gave a 3 by 3 grid where every row, column and diagonal added to 15.\n\"This is a magic square,\" she said."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "magic square",
          "sum",
          "trick"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "In a magic square the rows, columns and diagonals all have the same sum. The Lo Shu square uses 1 to 9 and each line adds to 15.\nNumber tricks use rules. Think of a number, double it, add 6, halve it and subtract your number. The answer is always 3.\nPlaying with numbers helps us spot patterns and reasons."
        }
